THE INVARIANTS ARE CYCLE PARITIES of H = K_n minus the base path.
  star flips generate the CUT space of H (dim n-1); the orthogonal complement is the CYCLE space.
  Claim: for every cycle C in H, the parity of the orientation bits around C is INVARIANT.

  n= 6 : 4 triangles of H tested, 4000 random (tiling, star-flip) trials -> parity changes: 0
  n= 7 : 6 triangles of H tested, 4000 random (tiling, star-flip) trials -> parity changes: 0
  n= 8 : 6 triangles of H tested, 4000 random (tiling, star-flip) trials -> parity changes: 0

  => cycle parities of H are EXACTLY conserved under every vertex-star (map-graph) flip.

  NESTED CUT/CYCLE STRUCTURE (new):
   level 1 (CLAUDE.md): K_n = cut(base path) + cycle(rel. path);  the TILES are that cycle space.
   level 2 (this):      inside the tile space, star flips = cut(H), invariants = cycle(H),
                        H = K_n minus the base path,  dim cut = n-1, dim cycle = C(n-1,2)-(n-1).
